UNIT mii_checksum
KIND FUNCTIONAL
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
FIDELITY spec
ANCHOR CRC-16/XMODEM in the CRC RevEng catalogue (width 16, poly 0x1021, init 0x0000, no reflection, xorout 0x0000, check 0x31C3), the checksum the last two bytes of a Wii U Mii hold
SIG mii_checksum(data: bytes) -> u64
ENVELOPE data is any byte string, the empty one included.
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION The checksum a Wii U Mii keeps in its last two bytes, computed over the bytes before them.
BEHAVIOR
R1 The answer is the CRC-16/XMODEM of data: polynomial 0x1021, starting value 0, bits taken most significant first, no reflection, nothing XORed at the end. CITED
R2 The answer is always between 0 and 65535.
R3 Empty data answers 0. The nine bytes of the text "123456789" answer 12739 (0x31C3). CITED
R4 Appending the answer to data as two bytes, most significant first, gives data whose checksum is 0.
PROVENANCE recorded by rdv from mii/mii.go
ORACLE value -> oracles/mii_checksum.json CANONICAL-SHA256 72e2c749014e7dcb0023759a21be292a619b4309cfff9a57fca4e81b145352b4
NOTE rules written; no independent rebuild has been graded yet.
